ight diffusion transformer architectures and closed enterprise cloud services. Evaluation centers on temporal consistency, motion fidelity, physics accuracy, and generation latency.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Alibaba's Wan 2.1 suite represents a major technical landmark for open-source video generation. Wan 2.1 utilizes a 3D Causal Variational Autoencoder (Wan-VAE) that achieves a 256\times spatiotemporal compression factor, converting continuous spatial and temporal dimensions into compact latent representations. Guided by an umT5 multilingual text encoder, the model's Diffusion Transformer (DiT) iteratively denoises video latents. The generation flow processes raw prompt or source image inputs through the umT5 or CLIP encoder to extract spatial and text embeddings, passes these embeddings into the Diffusion Transformer alongside the 3D causal Wan-VAE latent, iteratively denoises the latent representation, and finally decodes it through the Wan-VAE decoder into a rendered MP4 video file. Wan 2.1 is available in two distinct parameter sizes: a compact T2V-1.3B model optimized for 480p resolution on consumer GPUs, and a high-capacity 14B model supporting 480p and 720p output.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Tencent's HunyuanVideo provides a competing open-weight foundation model, offering video synthesis capabilities that run locally on enterprise GPU clusters or via managed APIs. On the hosted enterprise side, Google Veo 3 and Veo 3.1 offer generative video capabilities integrated into Vertex AI. Veo models generate cinematic 1080p clips with detailed camera control and motion stability, though at higher API costs.</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:78pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Video Model</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:78pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Parameter Scale</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:78pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-siz